# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the sanitizers job. None are needed: the job links libGLX (KEEP_GL in ci.yml), so
# glfwTerminate() can't unload Mesa's driver before the leak report, and the memory the driver keeps until exit is
# still reachable from its globals. If a Mesa update leaks for real, suppress it here by module (e.g.
# leak:libgallium), never by one of our functions, which would hide our own leaks under it too.
